            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0220" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/2414: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-01-04T15:00:00+08:00">January 4, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 4—2:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. My 108, December 27, 11 a.m.<anchor n="93" xml:id="d267-f1"/> Following
                    memorandum was handed me yesterday by the German Ambassador: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“According to a telegram from the German Embassy in Tokyo, the Japanese
                            Ministry for Foreign Affairs has pointed out that it would be nearly
                            impossible for airplanes to distinguish foreign houses marked with flag
                            and that in case of an air attack, the concentration of foreign
                            nationals in said zones formerly mentioned would therefore be
                            advisable.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">The telegram was in response to a message along the same lines
                    as my 33, December 13, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="94" xml:id="d267-f2"/> which the German
                    Ambassador sent to Tokyo in which he pointed out immediately that many
                    foreigners were living in houses likely to be with flags outside the notified
                    area.</p>
                <p>Sent to Peiping, Shanghai. Peiping please repeat to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
